Enhancement: explicit command lock policy foundation

Vaultic now represents command locking through `LockPolicy{None, Shared,
Exclusive}` instead of overloading dry-run and no-lock booleans. Read commands
can resolve to `None` through the Alpha lock-free read feature; append writers
use `Shared`; destructive and coherent-view commands use `Exclusive`.

The typed policy layer keeps actual dry-runs non-writing, prevents lock-free
mode from silently changing append operations into dry-runs, and preserves the
safe current boundary: lock-free reads, shared append locks, exclusive prune
and destructive operations. Tests cover policy resolution, lock-file creation
for reads/appends, writable no-lock backups, and repeated race-enabled
backup/prune/forget coordination.

